{"name":"Sneaky Devil","hex":"#840014","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sneaky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Elusive; difficult to capture or observe due to constantly outwitting the adversaries.","Dishonest; deceitful."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any device used for covert surveillance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneaky"},{"term":"devil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The chief devil; Satan."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evil creature, the objectification of a hostile and destructive force.","A man with red or orange skin and a pair of horns on his head, a pointed goatee, and a long tail, who carries a pitchfork, represents evil, and is portrayed to children as a boogeyman who punishes bad behavior."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Devil","blocks":[{"text":"The devil is a mythical personification of evil as conceived in various cultures and religious traditions. It is seen as the objectification of a hostile and destructive force. Jeffrey Burton Russell states that the different conceptions of the Devil can be summed up as 1. a principle of evil independent from God, 2. an aspect of God, 3. a created being turning evil or 4. a symbol of human evil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/022_devil_representation.JPG/330px-022_devil_representation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/120px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/250px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/12